[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+## How a loop runs[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+1. **Round 0 - the bar.** Lead writes `spec.md` (what "done" means, observable) and `eye.md` (how the real output is observed). Critic setup mode writes `rubric.md` (5-8 aspects, top-professional descriptors) and `checklist.md` (15-30 pass/fail lines with numbers).[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+2. **Round 1 - full build.** Every checklist line built in one round, complete first version, parallel builders.[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+3. **Rounds 2..N - judge / keep / batch.** Fresh critic each round: PASS/FAIL/UNSEEN per line with evidence, aspect scores vs best-so-far, at most 3 professional rejections. Lead keeps what passed, batches every FAIL + new line into the next build round.[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+4. **Stop.** Bar met (>=90% PASS, every aspect >=8, no open rejection), plateau, or budget (4 judged rounds default). Every stop without the bar met writes `BAR NOT MET` at the top of the report. The word "done" appears only when the bar is met.[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+[0m
